      "hints": [
        "General term is $\\binom{7}{r}(3x)^{7-r}(\\frac{2}{3x^2})^r$.",
        "Set power $7 - 3r = -2 \\implies r = 3$.",
        "Evaluate $\\binom{7}{3}(3^4)(\\frac{8}{27}) = 35 \\times 81 \\times \\frac{8}{27} = 840$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the general term in the binomial expansion of $\\left(3x + \\frac{2}{3x^2}\\right)^7$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{7}{r} (3x)^{7 - r} \\left(\\frac{2}{3x^2}\\right)^r = \\binom{7}{r} 3^{7 - r} \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^r x^{7 - 3r}$$",
        "Find the index $r$ for the term in $\\frac{1}{x^2} = x^{-2}$:\n$$7 - 3r = -2 \\implies 3r = 9 \\implies r = 3$$",
        "Substitute $r = 3$ to calculate the coefficient:\n$$\\text{Term} = \\binom{7}{3} (3x)^4 \\left(\\frac{2}{3x^2}\\right)^3 = 35 \\times 81x^4 \\times \\frac{8}{27x^6} = 840x^{-2}$$\n$$\\text{Coefficient of } \\frac{1}{x^2} = 840$$"
      ],
